diff --git a/docs/push-notifications.md b/docs/push-notifications.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9ade0d9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/push-notifications.md
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# Web push notifications
+
+Set `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` to a matching, URL-safe Base64
+VAPID key pair in both the web and job-worker environments. To generate a pair:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}"; puts "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+Keep the private key secret and keep the pair stable across deployments. Only
+the public key is sent to the browser. Run `bin/rails db:migrate` when upgrading.
+Without both keys, push delivery is disabled and settings explain that it is
+not configured; tray and email notifications continue working.
+
+Web push requires HTTPS (or localhost for development), a supported browser,
+and a running background-job worker. Users enable it in **Notification
+Settings → Push Notifications** on each device. On iOS, they may need to install
+the app on their home screen first; the settings page includes browser-specific
+help. Permission is requested only after clicking the enable button.
+
+Each account membership registers its own device subscription. Turning it off
+removes only that registration, not another device or another account using the
+same browser. Deactivating a user removes their subscriptions. Push-service
+responses indicating an expired or invalid subscription remove that device;
+temporary push-service failures are retried separately for each device.
+
+Pushes use the tray's text and account-scoped card/comment links. New activity
+on a grouped tray notification also sends a push; marking items read or unread
+does not.
+
+## Verification
+
+```sh
+bin/rails test test/controllers/users/push_subscriptions_controller_test.rb test/models/notification/pushable_test.rb test/models/push_subscription_test.rb
+bundle exec ruby test/javascript/push_notifications_test.rb
+```
+
+The JavaScript tests require Chrome/Chromium and Selenium. They mock browser
+push services; a live end-to-end check still requires real VAPID keys and a
+device granting notification permission.
diff --git a/test/controllers/users/push_subscriptions_controller_test.rb b/test/controllers/users/push_subscriptions_controller_test.rb
